<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE RUSSIAN TITLE OF THE TAB-BAR OVERFLOW TAB.

  A TabBar holding more than five items cannot show them all: MAUI's Android tab bar moves the rest
  into a built-in overflow tab, and that tab's title came out of Microsoft.Maui.Controls' own
  res/values/strings.xml as the literal " More ". It is not a Shell property, not a ShellContent
  Title, and nothing in AppShell.xaml.cs can set it. What MAUI reads is the ANDROID string resource
  `overflow_tab_title` from the app's own resources, so an app-level resource of that name replaces
  the library's — the same override mechanism styles.xml in this folder uses to redefine
  Maui.SplashTheme, and Android's normal rule that the app's value wins over a library's.

  «Ещё» is the ordinary Russian for "more", and it is the word a Russian Android device already
  uses for its own system tab overflow, so the operator reads the same word here as in the OS.

  WHY THE SHELL IS NOT RESTRUCTURED INSTEAD
  ==========================================
  Six tabs with a Russian overflow title leaves every section one tap away and does not touch the
  navigation tree at all, so nothing about LeaveOpenShiftAsync can regress. Every structural
  alternative costs something that matters more:

    · Three tabs, the other three sections in a FLYOUT. The flyout's hamburger is drawn in the Shell
      nav bar, and every top-level page in this app hides that bar (Shell.NavBarIsVisible="False" on
      MenuPage, OrdersPage, ShiftReportPage, ShiftAnalyticsPage, CatalogManagementPage, SettingsPage
      and OpenShiftPage). The drawer would have no visible opener anywhere, and the only way in would
      be an undocumented swipe from the screen edge.

    · Four tabs plus a HUB page listing the other three. The six sections still have to exist as
      ShellContent routes whatever happens to the tab bar, because ShiftReportViewModel opens the
      analytics report with GoToTabAsync("shift-analytics") (NavigationService turns it into
      "///shift-analytics") and NavigationService.LeaveOpenShiftAsync leaves the opening screen with
      GoToAsync("..") followed by "///menu". A hub would put three rows behind two taps and add a
      page plus a DI registration to get there.

    · SHORTER TITLES. The overflow tab appears because of how many items there are, not how wide
      their titles measure. No spelling of «Меню» removes it.

  PLATFORM SCOPE. This resource exists only in MAUI's Android build (verified: the string
  `overflow_tab_title` is present in Microsoft.Maui.Controls' net*-android assembly and in neither
  the iOS nor the Windows one). On iOS the overflow tab belongs to the OS, which labels it in the
  device language. On Windows nothing here applies; whether that build shows an overflow tab at all
  was not checked.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="overflow_tab_title">Ещё</string>
</resources>